-- ccc27-s737-surcharge.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, section 737 (victim surcharge).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.

§ `Section 737 -- Victim surcharge`

§§ `737(1) The duty to pay a victim surcharge`

-- The Acts named in section 737(1).
DECLARE `s 737(1) Act of the offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 737(1) this Act`
    `s 737(1) the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
    `s 737(1) the Cannabis Act`
    `s 737(1) some other Act`

-- src:15770 | 737 (1) An offender who is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence, in addition to any other punishment imposed on the offender.
@ref s 737(1) (src:15770)
GIVEN convicted IS A BOOLEAN
      `discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 737(1) Act of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(1) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (convicted OR `discharged under section 730`) AND NOT (act EQUALS `s 737(1) some other Act`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act"

§§ `737(2) The amount`

-- Meaning of "an offence punishable by summary conviction" and "an offence punishable by indictment" for a hybrid offence: the text is silent
-- (it says neither); this module takes the mode in which the offender was convicted (fork F-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:15772 | (2) Subject to subsections (2.1) and (3), the amount of the victim surcharge in respect of an offence is
-- src:15773 | (a) 30% of any fine that is imposed on the offender for the offence; or
-- src:15774 | (b) if no fine is imposed on the offender for the offence,
-- src:15775 | (i) $100 in the case of an offence punishable by summary conviction, and
-- src:15776 | (ii) $200 in the case of an offence punishable by indictment.
@ref s 737(2) (src:15772-15776)
GIVEN `s 734.8 the fine and its penalty` IS A Fine
      `the mode in which the offender was convicted` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 737(2) the amount of the victim surcharge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 734.8 the fine and its penalty`
    WHEN `a fine of` dollars THEN JUST (dollars TIMES 30%)   -- (a) 30% of any fine imposed
    WHEN `a fine in the discretion of the court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): no amount of fine is stated, so 30% cannot be computed
    WHEN `no fine is stated` THEN   -- (b) if no fine is imposed; a hybrid offence is taken in the mode of the conviction (fork F-1)
        CONSIDER `the mode in which the offender was convicted`
        WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST 100   -- (b)(i)
        WHEN `by indictment` THEN JUST 200   -- (b)(ii)

§§ `737(2.1) to (2.4) Reduction or waiver for undue hardship`

-- src:15784 | (2.3) For greater certainty, for the purposes of subsection (2.2), the imprisonment of the offender alone does not constitute undue hardship.
@ref s 737(2.3) (src:15784)
GIVEN `the only circumstance relied on is the imprisonment of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(2.3) the imprisonment of the offender alone constitutes undue hardship` MEANS
    IF `the only circumstance relied on is the imprisonment of the offender`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the imprisonment of the offender alone does not constitute undue hardship"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "alone"

-- src:15782 | (2.2) For the purposes of subsection (2.1), undue hardship means the offender is unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of the offender’s precarious financial circumstances, including because of their unemployment, homelessness, lack of assets or significant financial obligations towards their dependants.
@ref s 737(2.2) (src:15782)
GIVEN `the offender is unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of the offender's precarious financial circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only circumstance relied on is the imprisonment of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(2.2) undue hardship` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 737(2.3) the imprisonment of the offender alone constitutes undue hardship` `the only circumstance relied on is the imprisonment of the offender` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the imprisonment of the offender alone does not constitute undue hardship" (subsection (2.3))
        IF `the offender is unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of the offender's precarious financial circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "undue hardship means the offender is unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of the offender’s precarious financial circumstances"

-- The court's power to order no surcharge or a reduced one. Gate 1 is the application provision of subsection (8). Gate 2 is the "if it is satisfied" gate
-- of the subsection. The first limb takes the answer of s 737(2.2); the second limb is the court's own judgment, taken as an input.
-- src:15778 | (2.1) Despite subsection (1), the court may, on application of the offender or on its own motion, order an offender to pay no victim surcharge, or to pay a reduced amount, if it is satisfied that the victim surcharge
-- src:15779 | (a) would cause undue hardship to the offender; or
-- src:15780 | (b) would not cause undue hardship to the offender but would be disproportionate to the gravity of the offence or the degree of responsibility of the offender.
@ref s 737(2.1) (src:15778-15780)
GIVEN `the offence was committed after the day on which subsections (2.1) to (2.4) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `undue hardship, by s 737(2.2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the victim surcharge would be disproportionate to the gravity of the offence or the degree of responsibility of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(2.1) the court may order the offender to pay no victim surcharge, or a reduced amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offence was committed after the day on which subsections (2.1) to (2.4) came into force`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (8), "that was committed after the day on which those subsections come into force"
        IF `undue hardship, by s 737(2.2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF `undue hardship, by s 737(2.2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the court is satisfied that the victim surcharge would be disproportionate to the gravity of the offence or the degree of responsibility of the offender`
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b) "would not cause undue hardship to the offender but would be disproportionate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is satisfied that" (a grant named "may": fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:15786 | (2.4) When the court makes an order under subsection (2.1), the court shall state its reasons in the record of the proceedings.
@ref s 737(2.4) (src:15786)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under subsection (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(2.4) the court must state its reasons in the record of the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under subsection (2.1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the court makes an order under subsection (2.1)" (a duty whose "when" is unmet, fork F-3)

§§ `737(3) Increase`

-- src:15788 | (3) The court may order an offender to pay a victim surcharge in an amount exceeding that set out in subsection (2) if the court considers it appropriate in the circumstances and is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the higher amount.
@ref s 737(3) (src:15788)
GIVEN `the court considers it appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the higher amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(3) the court may order a victim surcharge exceeding the amount in subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the court considers it appropriate in the circumstances` AND `the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the higher amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court considers it appropriate in the circumstances and is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the higher amount" (a grant named "may": fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

§§ `737(4) and (5) Time for payment; where the money goes`

DECLARE `s 737(4) time for payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 737(4) within the time established by the lieutenant governor in council` HAS `the time, in days` IS A NUMBER
    `s 737(4) within a reasonable time after its imposition`

-- src:15790 | (4) The victim surcharge imposed in respect of an offence is payable within the time established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the surcharge is imposed. If no time has been so established, the surcharge is payable within a reasonable time after its imposition.
@ref s 737(4) (src:15790)
GIVEN `the time established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 737(4) time for payment`
`s 737(4) the time for payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province, in days`
    WHEN JUST days THEN `s 737(4) within the time established by the lieutenant governor in council` days
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 737(4) within a reasonable time after its imposition`

-- src:15790 | (4) The victim surcharge imposed in respect of an offence is payable within the time established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the surcharge is imposed. If no time has been so established, the surcharge is payable within a reasonable time after its imposition.
@ref s 737(4) (src:15790)
GIVEN `the day the surcharge was imposed` IS A DATE
      `the time established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 737(4) the last day for payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 737(4) the time for payment` `the time established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province, in days`
    WHEN `s 737(4) within the time established by the lieutenant governor in council` days
        THEN JUST (Date (DATE_DAY `the day the surcharge was imposed` PLUS days) (DATE_MONTH `the day the surcharge was imposed`) (DATE_YEAR `the day the surcharge was imposed`))
    WHEN `s 737(4) within a reasonable time after its imposition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "a reasonable time" is not a date

-- src:15792 | (5) A victim surcharge shall be applied for the purposes of providing such assistance to victims of offences as the lieutenant governor in council of the province in which the surcharge is imposed may direct from time to time.
@ref s 737(5) (src:15792)
GIVEN `the sum is a victim surcharge imposed under section 737` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(5) the sum is applied to the assistance to victims of offences that the lieutenant governor in council directs` MEANS
    IF `the sum is a victim surcharge imposed under section 737`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A victim surcharge shall be applied"

§§ `737(6) Notice`

-- src:15794 | (6) The court shall cause to be given to the offender a written notice setting out
-- src:15795 | (a) the amount of the victim surcharge;
-- src:15796 | (b) the manner in which the victim surcharge is to be paid;
-- src:15797 | (c) the time by which the victim surcharge must be paid; and
-- src:15798 | (d) the procedure for applying for a change in any terms referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c) in accordance with section 734.3.
@ref s 737(6) (src:15794-15798)
GIVEN `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the amount of the victim surcharge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the manner in which the victim surcharge is to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the time by which the victim surcharge must be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the procedure for applying for a change in the terms in paragraphs (b) and (c) in accordance with section 734.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(6) the notice is the written notice the court shall cause to be given` MEANS
    IF `the notice is in writing` AND `it sets out the amount of the victim surcharge` AND `it sets out the manner in which the victim surcharge is to be paid`
       AND `it sets out the time by which the victim surcharge must be paid`
       AND `it sets out the procedure for applying for a change in the terms in paragraphs (b) and (c) in accordance with section 734.3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a written notice setting out (a) the amount ... (b) ... (c) ... and (d) ..." (a list joined by "and") (fork F-14)

DECLARE `s 737(6) act` IS ONE OF `s 737(6) give the offender the written notice`

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the court acts, once, with no time limit stated in the text.
-- src:15794 | (6) The court shall cause to be given to the offender a written notice setting out
@ref s 737(6) (src:15794)
`s 737(6) the court shall cause the notice to be given` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 737(6) give the offender the written notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the written notice required by section 737(6) was not given to the offender"

§§ `737(7) Enforcement`

-- src:15800 | (7) Subsections 734(3) to (7) and sections 734.3, 734.5, 734.7, 734.8 and 736 apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in respect of a victim surcharge imposed under this section and, in particular,
@ref s 737(7) (src:15800)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(7) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a victim surcharge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision's `section` EQUALS 734 AND elem (provision's `subsection`) (LIST "(3)", "(4)", "(5)", "(6)", "(7)") THEN JUST TRUE   -- "subsections 734(3) to (7)"
        IF elem (provision's `section`) (LIST 734.3, 734.5, 734.7, 734.8, 736) THEN JUST TRUE   -- "sections 734.3, 734.5, 734.7, 734.8 and 736"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list names what applies and does not say that nothing else does; a decimal subsection between 734(3) and 734(7) is not named here

-- src:15801 | (a) a reference in any of those provisions to “fine”, other than in subsection 734.8(5), must be read as if it were a reference to “victim surcharge”; and
@ref s 737(7)(a) (src:15801)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(7)(a) the reference to fine in the provision is read as a reference to victim surcharge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision's `section` EQUALS 734.8 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(5)"
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than in subsection 734.8(5)" (fork F-15)
        IF `s 737(7) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a victim surcharge` provision EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks only of "any of those provisions"

-- src:15802 | (b) the notice provided under subsection (6) is deemed to be an order made under section 734.1.
@ref s 737(7)(b) (src:15802)
GIVEN `the notice is the notice provided under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(7)(b) the notice is deemed to be an order made under section 734.1` MEANS
    IF `the notice is the notice provided under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the notice provided under subsection (6)"

§§ `737(8) Application of subsections (2.1) to (2.4)`

-- src:15804 | (8) Subsections (2.1) to (2.4) apply to any offender who is sentenced for an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act that was committed after the day on which those subsections come into force.
@ref s 737(8) (src:15804)
GIVEN `the offender is sentenced for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 737(1) Act of the offence`
      `the offence was committed after the day on which subsections (2.1) to (2.4) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 737(8) subsections (2.1) to (2.4) apply to the offender` MEANS
    IF `the offender is sentenced for an offence` AND NOT (act EQUALS `s 737(1) some other Act`)
       AND `the offence was committed after the day on which subsections (2.1) to (2.4) came into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to any offender who is sentenced for an offence under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act that was committed after the day" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))
